      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/wall_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A Pennsylvania Railroad station opened in the early 1840s and was named Walls' Station in honor of the local Walls family.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wall%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "European settlement in Wall began in the 1760s, attracted by rich natural resources like fertile soils and abundant game for hunting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/wall_pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community of Wall was officially incorporated as a borough in 1904 after separating from North Versailles Township.",
